  "secondary_contrast_caveat": "angle_to_cw_pca_* is computed by methods.basis_whitened, whose raw-plus-factored branch -- reached only by Iso-MPCA -- unstacks a (C*T, rank) basis with B.reshape(rank, C, T, order='F') instead of B.T.reshape(...). That has the right shape but interleaves the basis index with the channel index, so Iso-MPCA's angle columns are computed from a scrambled basis. Round 9 discovered this while implementing E8 and deliberately did NOT change the function, because doing so would silently redefine an archived Block A column and break comparability between these replication rows and seeds 0-9. The two PRIMARY contrasts (test_normalized_chi2, test_raw_mse) do not use this function and are unaffected. The desk should decide whether to recompute the angle diagnostic for both subsets with the corrected convention; see r9_semantics.fitted_basis_whitened.",
  "secondary_contrast_is": "angle_to_cw_pca_mean_deg",
  "sign_convention": "All contrasts are NFPA minus Iso-MPCA on held-out test metrics. Negative favours NFPA for the two error metrics."
